Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [works around a libgomp defect on the riscv64 runners, riseproject-dev/python-wheels#617]

libgomp's dynamic and guided work-share schedules fault on the riscv64
machines these wheels are built and tested on (gotcha 166; the same
defect is worked around for lightgbm and healpy). phono3py's tests
segfaulted inside imag_self_energy_with_g() (a schedule(guided) loop),
in test_kappa_LBTE_rust_vs_c_sigma on cp313 and
test_kappa_LBTE_rust_vs_c_multi_sigma on cp312, while cp314/cp314t
passed the whole suite; the same tests run clean under AddressSanitizer
on x86_64 with 64 OpenMP threads. Move all seven schedule(guided) loops
under c/ to schedule(static), which only costs load balancing. Revert
once the runner toolchain is fixed.
